WEBVTT

00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:10.400
2808 A.D.

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:37.880
Number 813, it's time
for your interview.

00:00:40.810 --> 00:00:43.440
Number 867, it's time.

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:50.520
Number 851, it's time.

00:00:53.770 --> 00:00:56.440
I need an immediate decision.

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:02.480
Will you spend the rest of
your lives in this orbital prison,

00:01:02.610 --> 00:01:05.240
or become agents of the Cyber Police?

00:01:05.380 --> 00:01:09.070
You mean, serve as your trained hounds?

00:01:09.220 --> 00:01:12.880
Either way, we'll never be free.

00:01:13.010 --> 00:01:18.160
Not true. For every Type A
cyber criminal you apprehend,

00:01:18.290 --> 00:01:21.320
your sentences will be
reduced by a few years.

00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:24.640
Some day, you might
even earn your freedom.

00:01:24.730 --> 00:01:28.680
It all depends on how efficient you are.

00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:31.090
What a load of crap!

00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:33.920
At least it will end the boredom.

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:37.080
Besides, the stars are
right for a new venture.

00:01:37.220 --> 00:01:42.560
I'm in, too. Anything to
get another taste of freedom.

00:01:42.650 --> 00:01:50.040
Prisoner 813, Shunsuke Sengoku,
what is your decision?

00:01:50.130 --> 00:01:54.080
If you're ready to work for me,
take your baton.

00:01:57.250 --> 00:01:59.440
Don't worry, Hasegawa,

00:02:00.570 --> 00:02:02.920
I'm swallowing the bait.

00:02:05.690 --> 00:02:07.760
Have a good laugh.

00:02:28.530 --> 00:02:28.930
<b>SHUNSUKE SENGOKU</b>

00:02:28.940 --> 00:02:31.210
From deep within the darkest
corners of the night,

00:02:36.730 --> 00:02:37.450
<b>Oh, we're gonna take the
answer; make, make me down.</b>

00:02:37.460 --> 00:02:38.380
<b>MERRILL</b> YANAGAWA

00:02:38.380 --> 00:02:40.180
<b>Oh, we're gonna take the
answer; make, make me down.</b>

00:02:45.620 --> 00:02:46.130
I hear a voice I cannot,
no, will not forget.

00:02:46.130 --> 00:02:47.000
<b>GABIMARU</b> RIKIYA

00:02:50.650 --> 00:02:51.050
I'm running away from flash
lights; what, what is wrong?

00:02:55.290 --> 00:02:58.410
<b>Once there was a dark night,</b>

00:02:58.410 --> 00:03:01.730
When we loved each other,

00:03:01.730 --> 00:03:06.530
So desperate, yet so sad,

00:03:06.530 --> 00:03:12.120
Never to return.

00:03:13.340 --> 00:03:16.280
<b>Lonely game, silly game,</b>

00:03:16.620 --> 00:03:19.820
There can be no retreat
from night and day!

00:03:19.820 --> 00:03:21.420
Endless game,

00:03:21.420 --> 00:03:26.210
Hold on tightly
to your broken dreams.

00:03:26.530 --> 00:03:29.610
Follow me, stay with me,

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:33.010
<b>Last chance,
time to risk it all!</b>

00:03:33.010 --> 00:03:37.050
It's so hard,

00:03:37.060 --> 00:03:40.570
Baby, let me go.

00:03:41.050 --> 00:03:42.600
Just Burning World!

00:04:21.730 --> 00:04:24.680
Varsus, raise the drawbridge.

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:28.290
Please Justify the requested action.

00:04:28.420 --> 00:04:31.530
Do it fast if you don't
want him to get away.

00:04:32.890 --> 00:04:39.070
<b>Understood. Cyber Police
override on Bay Bridge 13.</b>

00:05:30.410 --> 00:05:31.630
<b>Go to hell!</b>

00:05:42.100 --> 00:05:45.880
Too bad. The profit from
your black market data...

00:05:46.020 --> 00:05:48.850
won't do you much
good in an orbital prison.

00:05:50.330 --> 00:05:51.470
<b>God damned hound!</b>

00:06:05.010 --> 00:06:08.240
<b>Request backup at Bay Bridge 13.</b>

00:06:08.380 --> 00:06:12.970
Hold your position until backup arrives.

00:06:12.980 --> 00:06:13.810
<b>Roger.</b>

00:06:15.690 --> 00:06:20.080
<b>Mission completed.
Are you inJured, Sengoku?</b>

00:06:20.210 --> 00:06:25.480
What a headache.
That vodka last night was terrible.

00:06:26.380 --> 00:06:30.930
Drinking is a violation of police
regulations, article <b>9.</b>

00:06:31.050 --> 00:06:34.000
Alcohol may impair performance
in critical situations.

00:06:35.210 --> 00:06:38.600
Have I ever let it
affect my performance?

00:06:38.740 --> 00:06:42.120
You'd never understand,
you pile of Junk.

00:06:42.260 --> 00:06:45.050
The advised cure for
a hangover is sleep.

00:06:45.180 --> 00:06:47.600
Thanks for the news flash.

00:08:30.980 --> 00:08:35.000
<b>Memories of the Past</b>

00:09:05.890 --> 00:09:08.120
Answer me, dammit!

00:09:08.250 --> 00:09:10.710
Sorry, I had problems finding my neck.

00:09:10.850 --> 00:09:15.240
You have 24 hours.
Then your collar will explode,

00:09:15.370 --> 00:09:18.880
and you won't be able to
tell any more stupid Jokes.

00:09:19.010 --> 00:09:23.720
Fine. If it cures my hangover,
blow my head right off.

00:09:23.850 --> 00:09:26.520
Your choice. I expect you
at the station, immediately.

00:09:28.690 --> 00:09:30.080
Damn him!

00:09:37.060 --> 00:09:38.760
Traffic <b>update:</b> delay in Zone 7-1

00:09:55.050 --> 00:09:59.720
Your performance on yesterday's
case has been evaluated.

00:10:00.860 --> 00:10:03.130
You received 3 years,
6 months of credit.

00:10:03.250 --> 00:10:07.600
Your remaining term is now
only 312 years, 4 months.

00:10:07.850 --> 00:10:12.210
Pile of Junk! How many more
people do I have to arrest...

00:10:12.220 --> 00:10:15.090
before this God damned
collar comes off?

00:10:15.370 --> 00:10:16.510
Insufficient data.

00:10:24.770 --> 00:10:26.920
These are the pertinent files.

00:10:28.420 --> 00:10:29.390
You're late.

00:10:30.420 --> 00:10:35.680
I thought traffic Jams were
a thing of the past. What's up?

00:10:36.370 --> 00:10:39.480
We're evacuating the space-scraper.

00:10:39.620 --> 00:10:40.810
Why?

00:10:40.930 --> 00:10:44.000
Someone hacked into the
building's main computer system.

00:10:47.380 --> 00:10:54.450
The primary systems included
military-level hardening.

00:10:54.540 --> 00:10:58.770
Evidence indicates massive
infiltration by an unknown virus.

00:10:58.890 --> 00:11:02.430
Have they made any moves
on the rest of Oedo?

00:11:02.580 --> 00:11:04.810
We haven't received any demands yet.

00:11:04.810 --> 00:11:06.610
But he has hostages in the main
computer room and elevators.

00:11:14.250 --> 00:11:18.120
It's your Job to catch him.
You have 24 hours.

00:11:21.410 --> 00:11:27.800
If he kills the main computer,
every network in Oedo will crash.

00:11:27.930 --> 00:11:31.800
The leeches and maggots of
this city would have a field day.

00:11:31.940 --> 00:11:33.810
Do we have any leads?

00:11:33.940 --> 00:11:37.810
Scanning the suspect database.

00:11:37.930 --> 00:11:40.640
<b>Goggles and Benten are
already on the Job.</b>

00:11:40.780 --> 00:11:42.800
Put your heads together
and solve this one fast.

00:11:44.260 --> 00:11:46.850
Do you ever get tired
of manipulating people?

00:11:50.370 --> 00:11:54.920
I've set your collar's timer
for 23 hours, 16 minutes.

00:11:55.060 --> 00:11:59.360
After that, there's going
to be three missing heads.

00:11:59.700 --> 00:12:01.800
No, four.

00:12:04.100 --> 00:12:07.080
I'll personally make sure there's
a fourth head to Join them.

00:12:57.220 --> 00:12:59.590
What a Joke.

00:12:59.690 --> 00:13:05.760
We built a monstrous city,
then we put the computers in charge.

00:13:05.890 --> 00:13:10.520
We rely too much on you
damn machines, don't we, Junkpile?

00:13:12.860 --> 00:13:16.240
All of these mechanisms
are human creations.

00:13:16.380 --> 00:13:19.360
All machines are merely
responding to human direction.

00:13:20.380 --> 00:13:25.530
<b>Maybe, but Just look at this place!</b>

00:13:25.650 --> 00:13:28.760
It's completely insane.

00:13:34.530 --> 00:13:36.760
Do you have the anti-virus software?

00:13:36.900 --> 00:13:39.270
Downloading now.

00:13:39.370 --> 00:13:40.760
How about the new system files?

00:13:40.900 --> 00:13:42.780
Download complete.

00:13:42.780 --> 00:13:46.040
Wait. Files 2 and 3 have been infected.

00:13:46.170 --> 00:13:48.730
All passwords have been compromised.

00:13:48.740 --> 00:13:52.320
They're intercepting all outside data.

00:13:52.500 --> 00:13:54.050
No good.

00:13:54.050 --> 00:13:54.060
How's it going, Goggles?
No good.

00:13:54.060 --> 00:13:55.960
How's it going, Goggles?

00:13:56.500 --> 00:13:58.050
This is fascinating.

00:13:58.330 --> 00:14:03.160
It's like chess.
A checkmate is inevitable.

00:14:03.300 --> 00:14:04.810
<b>Our opponent is a genius.</b>

00:14:04.940 --> 00:14:09.240
Just do something,
while we still have our heads.

00:14:09.330 --> 00:14:17.240
<b>Most computers use a password
to prevent unauthorized access.</b>

00:14:17.380 --> 00:14:22.960
This guy cracked the passwords
in a matter of seconds.

00:14:23.100 --> 00:14:27.850
This data provides no new
correlations in the database.

00:14:29.060 --> 00:14:31.400
How about defensive software?

00:14:31.530 --> 00:14:35.920
We tried, but the system blocked us out.

00:14:36.050 --> 00:14:39.640
We still have 100 million
combinations to try.

00:14:40.530 --> 00:14:42.830
Doesn't sound good.

00:14:42.980 --> 00:14:47.000
<b>Okyo is one of the elevator hostages.
Cheer her up.</b>

00:14:47.660 --> 00:14:49.080
She is?

00:14:49.220 --> 00:14:52.330
She was helping with the
evacuation but she got trapped.

00:14:57.340 --> 00:14:59.710
Jonouchi speaking.

00:14:59.810 --> 00:15:01.360
This is Sengoku.

00:15:01.500 --> 00:15:02.880
Sengoku!

00:15:03.010 --> 00:15:05.080
How are you doing?

00:15:06.500 --> 00:15:09.410
All fifteen of us are fine.

00:15:09.490 --> 00:15:15.240
<b>Good. You'll be back to your
paperwork tomorrow. Trust me.</b>

00:15:15.330 --> 00:15:17.360
I trust you.

00:15:17.500 --> 00:15:18.280
<b>Later.</b>

00:15:19.740 --> 00:15:23.720
Nice Job. It doesn't look
so bad after all.

00:15:23.850 --> 00:15:26.080
<b>Maybe I should have told her.</b>

00:15:26.170 --> 00:15:30.600
She's barely out of the Academy.
She's too young to die.

00:15:32.460 --> 00:15:34.920
How many hostages in
the main computer room?

00:15:35.420 --> 00:15:36.470
Just one.

00:15:37.380 --> 00:15:40.250
He's the systems supervisor,
Dave Kurokawa.

00:15:41.050 --> 00:15:45.720
He's super-elite, one of the most
important people in Oedo.

00:15:45.860 --> 00:15:49.610
But we can't reach him.
He's cut off from all outside contact.

00:15:49.970 --> 00:15:54.200
This stinks. That's a perfect
place for the criminal, too.

00:15:54.340 --> 00:15:57.530
We can't get in. The hallway
has anti-personnel lasers,

00:15:57.650 --> 00:16:02.480
which are hidden
behind armored shutters.

00:16:02.610 --> 00:16:06.200
And we're locked out
of the security systems.

00:16:07.340 --> 00:16:09.170
This <b>REALLY</b> stinks.

00:16:09.260 --> 00:16:13.410
That's what Benten said.
You two think alike.

00:16:24.180 --> 00:16:26.240
Close shave.

00:16:31.850 --> 00:16:34.600
Varsus, what's the delay
between beam sweeps?

00:16:39.540 --> 00:16:45.400
Each sweep is.75 seconds;
delay is.25 seconds.

00:16:45.530 --> 00:16:47.560
How long will my laser shield last?

00:16:47.700 --> 00:16:52.210
After 3.02 seconds all
power will be exhausted.

00:16:52.300 --> 00:16:56.960
Distance to computer room <b>door:</b>
67 meters, 20 centimeters.

00:17:08.500 --> 00:17:10.240
You could spend all day at this.

00:17:11.250 --> 00:17:12.640
I need a Nambu & Luger.

00:17:12.780 --> 00:17:15.720
Weapon <b>access:</b> granted.

00:17:15.980 --> 00:17:18.490
Hurry it up.

00:17:18.620 --> 00:17:20.320
Fingerprint lock, verified.

00:17:23.290 --> 00:17:24.760
Now get that grate.

00:17:26.330 --> 00:17:32.040
<b>Good. We've finally found
decent work for you.</b>

00:17:56.980 --> 00:17:59.350
Shit. It's going to ram me!

00:18:01.300 --> 00:18:04.640
Where's mobility control on
a maintenance robot?

00:18:05.050 --> 00:18:08.800
A type <b>AU-</b> 50 robot, or an Iwata-896?

00:18:08.930 --> 00:18:10.360
How should I know?

00:18:10.490 --> 00:18:12.870
Type <b>AU:</b> the upper right side.

00:18:16.010 --> 00:18:20.000
The <b>896</b> has the control
on the end of its arm,

00:18:20.140 --> 00:18:25.570
an improvement on
the older type <b>459</b> robot.

00:18:25.700 --> 00:18:30.530
However, the type <b>AU-</b> 50 is
still the most popular model.

00:18:52.170 --> 00:18:54.280
Dave Kurokawa, I presume?

00:18:54.410 --> 00:18:56.240
Who are you?

00:18:57.860 --> 00:19:00.280
I'm with the police.
I'm here to rescue you.

00:19:06.170 --> 00:19:07.200
<b>Rescue me?</b>

00:19:13.610 --> 00:19:15.000
What's so funny?

00:19:15.290 --> 00:19:19.890
This is hilarious!
Where could we possibly go?

00:19:19.890 --> 00:19:26.070
There's nowhere to run.
This is the safest place I could be.

00:19:27.540 --> 00:19:28.840
What do you mean?

00:19:32.060 --> 00:19:36.080
I've locked out every
system in this area.

00:19:36.220 --> 00:19:38.170
I'm one step ahead of him.

00:19:39.690 --> 00:19:41.640
You know who's behind this?

00:19:42.890 --> 00:19:48.600
You'd never catch him.
You police are such incompetents!

00:19:49.900 --> 00:19:52.690
I don't know; we're pretty
good with parking tickets.

00:19:54.010 --> 00:19:58.720
It won't do you any good,
but if you really want to know...

00:19:59.290 --> 00:20:01.920
The systems have been taken
over by Yoshikazu Amachi.

00:20:02.060 --> 00:20:03.340
Do you have proof?

00:20:03.340 --> 00:20:06.880
He helped design this building.

00:20:07.260 --> 00:20:10.170
He's the only one who could
manage something like this.

00:20:11.740 --> 00:20:15.280
Varsus, run a check on
a man named Yoshikazu Amachi.

00:20:15.570 --> 00:20:16.480
<b>Understood.</b>

00:20:17.730 --> 00:20:23.880
What's going on? The security
systems are back on line!

00:20:26.100 --> 00:20:28.760
The cracker must be working
inside the building!

00:20:30.260 --> 00:20:32.530
Impossible!

00:20:32.980 --> 00:20:35.080
Trace these new transmissions!

00:20:39.290 --> 00:20:46.600
Yoshikazu <b>Amachi:</b> Australian
citizen of Japanese descent.

00:20:46.690 --> 00:20:54.960
Developed software techniques
used in the control of Oedo.

00:20:55.890 --> 00:21:03.440
High ranking member of the
space-scraper development team.

00:21:03.580 --> 00:21:09.160
Yoshikazu Amachi was
declared missing in 2793.

00:21:10.170 --> 00:21:12.960
No one's seen him in fifteen years.

00:21:13.580 --> 00:21:18.840
I know that, but he's somewhere in Oedo.
You have to find him!

00:21:51.060 --> 00:21:54.440
Warning

00:21:54.580 --> 00:21:56.370
<b>Give me Kurokawa.</b>

00:21:56.370 --> 00:21:56.380
<b>Give me Kurokawa.
Kurokawa?
Give me Kurokawa.</b>

00:21:56.380 --> 00:21:57.430
<b>Give me Kurokawa.
Kurokawa?</b>

00:21:59.050 --> 00:22:01.330
Was he after you all along?

00:22:01.330 --> 00:22:02.680
Warning

00:22:19.020 --> 00:22:21.440
Varsus, the hostage elevator
is dropping! Stop it!

00:23:07.620 --> 00:23:12.480
That's quite a warning.
This guy really wants you dead.

00:23:12.970 --> 00:23:15.160
Why is he after you?

00:23:17.620 --> 00:23:20.680
I don't have to tell you.

00:23:23.100 --> 00:23:25.660
Stay back or I'll kill you!

00:23:33.900 --> 00:23:38.450
Idiot. This gun has a fingerprint lock.

00:23:38.650 --> 00:23:41.960
It's a useless hunk of
metal to anyone but me.

00:23:43.100 --> 00:23:45.520
But I'd be happy to
demonstrate it for you.

00:23:45.940 --> 00:23:50.010
I bet Amachi would thank
me for saving him the trouble.

00:23:50.220 --> 00:23:52.170
And you call yourself a police officer?

00:23:52.690 --> 00:23:57.600
Sort of, but I'm still working off
a few life sentences.

00:23:59.050 --> 00:24:02.080
Do you think you can get away with this?

00:24:02.450 --> 00:24:05.480
If you want to live, start talking.

00:24:06.820 --> 00:24:08.920
Why is Amachi after you?

00:24:12.340 --> 00:24:14.440
Amachi was a genius.

00:24:18.180 --> 00:24:22.170
We worked on the
computer systems together,

00:24:22.170 --> 00:24:26.040
during the space-scraper's construction.

00:24:27.620 --> 00:24:33.410
But Amachi was always better than I was.

00:24:34.290 --> 00:24:37.490
They were going to make him
one of the super-elite.

00:24:37.490 --> 00:24:40.520
But if I eliminated him,
they'd give that rank to me.

00:24:41.300 --> 00:24:42.770
So I did it. I killed him.

00:24:44.500 --> 00:24:48.930
Fifteen years ago,
in this very building.

00:24:57.180 --> 00:24:59.370
I'm sure I killed him.

00:25:01.820 --> 00:25:03.920
He couldn't still be alive, could he?

00:25:05.490 --> 00:25:07.720
It's been fifteen years,

00:25:07.810 --> 00:25:10.160
and now he's come for revenge!

00:25:10.300 --> 00:25:12.920
He's come back from the dead,
Just to get me!

00:25:24.450 --> 00:25:26.160
I don't believe it!

00:25:28.100 --> 00:25:30.610
Varsus, connect me to Sengoku.

00:25:30.930 --> 00:25:31.880
<b>Understood.</b>

00:25:32.610 --> 00:25:33.670
Sengoku here.

00:25:34.250 --> 00:25:37.790
I've pinpointed the transmissions.
<b>Ready for this?</b>

00:25:37.980 --> 00:25:40.850
He's inside the building.

00:25:42.610 --> 00:25:44.440
<b>Right under our noses.</b>

00:25:44.570 --> 00:25:47.800
He's at the far end of corridor 63.

00:25:47.890 --> 00:25:50.000
<b>Okay, I'll get him.</b>

00:25:52.010 --> 00:25:54.960
Watch out.
There's something weird about this.

00:25:55.100 --> 00:25:57.470
We don't know what he's capable of.

00:25:57.570 --> 00:26:01.320
<b>Maybe not, but I'm going to finish this.</b>

00:26:01.420 --> 00:26:03.120
I owe this guy.

00:26:09.290 --> 00:26:12.520
Turn off the security outside this room.

00:26:13.460 --> 00:26:15.730
And then, start praying.

00:26:20.770 --> 00:26:24.290
Don't Just stand there.
We've got work to do!

00:26:24.290 --> 00:26:26.920
<b>Our target is in corridor 63.</b>

00:26:32.620 --> 00:26:36.090
I don't like this.
The stars are not auspicious.

00:26:42.300 --> 00:26:43.960
An outbound transmission!

00:26:44.380 --> 00:26:45.520
From where?

00:26:47.660 --> 00:26:51.770
3F-102. The satellite control dish.

00:27:06.060 --> 00:27:09.400
He's using the satellite laser cannon
to destroy the building!

00:27:11.890 --> 00:27:13.110
He's insane!

00:27:15.620 --> 00:27:19.130
<b>Okay, route everything you've got
through my station.</b>

00:27:32.140 --> 00:27:33.970
Want to take a taxi?

00:27:33.970 --> 00:27:33.980
Sure. I bet they'd
take us straight to hell.
Want to take a taxi?

00:27:33.980 --> 00:27:36.800
Sure. I bet they'd
take us straight to hell.

00:27:59.330 --> 00:28:00.970
There's too many.

00:28:00.970 --> 00:28:03.350
Benten, handle the
traffic control for me.

00:28:40.860 --> 00:28:43.370
He's turned off the gyro-stabilizer.

00:28:43.500 --> 00:28:46.650
The space-scraper's starting to tilt!

00:28:56.220 --> 00:28:58.920
Emergency evacuation!
Clear the area!

00:29:06.330 --> 00:29:09.240
Stop it, Amachi! Stop!

00:29:43.100 --> 00:29:44.200
This is Hasegawa.

00:29:44.490 --> 00:29:47.050
I'd love to chat, but I'm kind of busy.

00:29:47.130 --> 00:29:50.120
I recorded Dave Kurokawa's confession.

00:29:50.260 --> 00:29:51.530
Execute him.

00:29:51.650 --> 00:29:52.870
What?

00:29:53.010 --> 00:29:58.360
<b>Kill him. He's responsible for the
current threat to Oedo.</b>

00:29:58.490 --> 00:30:02.110
Why bother? Let the courts handle him.

00:30:02.260 --> 00:30:06.330
I was in charge of the
Amachi case 15 years ago.

00:30:06.460 --> 00:30:10.690
Pressure from Kurokawa
halted the investigation.

00:30:11.100 --> 00:30:13.890
He should have paid
for his crimes 15 years ago.

00:30:17.900 --> 00:30:20.770
I don't have time for your sob stories.

00:30:20.890 --> 00:30:23.840
I'm going to settle things with Amachi.

00:30:23.980 --> 00:30:27.670
This is an order. Kurokawa's
death will end the crisis.

00:30:27.770 --> 00:30:30.400
Do it or I'll blow your head off!

00:30:30.970 --> 00:30:34.840
I don't like the way either
you or Amachi work.

00:30:37.530 --> 00:30:39.360
Both of you...

00:30:39.450 --> 00:30:40.560
can go to hell!

00:31:27.540 --> 00:31:31.440
Varsus, how many blocks in corridor 63?

00:31:31.570 --> 00:31:33.930
12 blocks.

00:31:33.930 --> 00:31:36.760
Are you positive?
<b>Of course you are...</b>

00:31:38.580 --> 00:31:42.270
We're short one block.

00:31:55.370 --> 00:31:57.440
That explains it.

00:32:16.020 --> 00:32:18.120
What's that?

00:32:49.820 --> 00:32:51.090
Amachi!

00:33:37.420 --> 00:33:42.040
It's a simulation.
He's predicting my moves.

00:34:02.820 --> 00:34:04.690
He has the satellite!

00:34:18.930 --> 00:34:21.390
Damn machine!

00:34:23.900 --> 00:34:27.560
Time for some new input!

00:34:53.860 --> 00:34:56.730
Try to compute this,

00:34:56.820 --> 00:34:58.520
you bastard!

00:35:37.370 --> 00:35:38.800
Sengoku!

00:35:45.380 --> 00:35:49.250
Varsus, mission accomplished.
Tell the kennel master.

00:35:49.330 --> 00:35:52.280
<b>Kennel master? Meaning unclear.</b>

00:35:52.370 --> 00:35:56.150
There is no identification
attached to that phrase.

00:35:56.300 --> 00:35:57.270
Figure it out.

00:36:37.780 --> 00:36:41.360
I can't believe it!
Why didn't my sentence go down?

00:36:41.490 --> 00:36:45.240
<b>Repeating:</b> You ignored
orders while on a critical case,

00:36:45.370 --> 00:36:48.170
resulting in a demerit of
10 years, 6 months.

00:36:48.180 --> 00:36:52.250
Your total term is now
315 years, 2 months.

00:36:52.380 --> 00:36:55.900
<b>Give up, Sengoku.
You can't argue with Varsus.</b>

00:36:55.900 --> 00:37:01.090
I agree. We saved the city,
and we still have our heads.

00:37:01.220 --> 00:37:05.000
As long as we're alive,
we can still get out of this.

00:37:05.570 --> 00:37:07.090
<b>Mind your own business.</b>

00:37:07.090 --> 00:37:10.840
<b>Listen you pile of Junk,
I'm going to sell you for scrap.</b>

00:37:11.540 --> 00:37:14.130
Think of me when they
start recycling your parts.

00:37:15.290 --> 00:37:20.200
That's when you'll regret being a
heartless piece of Junk.

00:37:20.340 --> 00:37:23.490
Sengoku, I'm glad I found you!

00:37:24.660 --> 00:37:27.450
What should I put in this space?

00:37:29.220 --> 00:37:33.600
Yoshikazu Amachi died 15 years ago.

00:37:33.740 --> 00:37:35.530
So how can he be responsible?

00:37:35.530 --> 00:37:35.540
Ask the Junkpile.
So how can he be responsible?

00:37:35.540 --> 00:37:37.000
Ask the Junkpile.

00:37:37.770 --> 00:37:44.200
Varsus said he doesn't know!
How should I fill this in?

00:37:44.890 --> 00:37:47.160
Write, "Insufficient data."

00:37:48.490 --> 00:37:51.080
Amachi died years ago.

00:37:51.220 --> 00:37:54.010
Somehow, his consciousness
survived in the computer.

00:37:54.140 --> 00:37:59.570
Amachi programmed it
to take revenge on Kurokawa.

00:37:59.700 --> 00:38:02.040
How can you explain that in a report?

00:38:03.090 --> 00:38:05.470
There's only one thing I'm sure <b>of:</b>

00:38:05.580 --> 00:38:09.410
When Kurokawa died,
Amachi was finally satisfied.

00:38:09.540 --> 00:38:12.480
Nothing we did could have stopped that.

00:38:13.170 --> 00:38:15.120
Quite a mystery.

00:38:18.700 --> 00:38:20.170
Yeah.

00:38:21.620 --> 00:38:24.410
Sengoku, want to get something to eat?

00:38:24.570 --> 00:38:30.910
No, thanks. It's hard
to relax with this collar on.

00:38:31.900 --> 00:38:34.410
I'll massage your neck for you!

00:38:35.940 --> 00:38:40.600
Thanks, but not today.

00:38:45.660 --> 00:38:49.640
I'd rather blow this thing off.

00:38:50.290 --> 00:38:53.830
But first, I'll get rid of this city's
parasites and scum.

00:39:42.220 --> 00:39:51.890
It may be true that
I may be in love with you,

00:39:53.130 --> 00:40:01.440
If I unwrap my heart
and see what's inside.

00:40:04.420 --> 00:40:13.960
It may be that I have
been wand'ring around lost,

00:40:15.140 --> 00:40:22.960
Hiding my true feelings
from everyone.

00:40:27.140 --> 00:40:32.000
Never to see you anymore,

00:40:32.570 --> 00:40:37.000
Has turned out to be so painful for me.

00:40:38.170 --> 00:40:43.400
Before time moves on without us,

00:40:43.540 --> 00:40:47.920
And takes you away forever,

00:40:49.130 --> 00:40:54.600
I Just want to say I love you,

00:40:54.730 --> 00:40:58.920
Ever so gently I whisper.

00:41:03.060 --> 00:41:08.400
Before time moves on without us,

00:41:08.540 --> 00:41:12.920
And takes you away forever,

00:41:14.060 --> 00:41:19.450
I Just want to say I love you,

00:41:19.580 --> 00:41:23.960
Ever so gently I whisper.

00:41:25.060 --> 00:41:30.570
Putting my trust and faith in you,

00:41:30.700 --> 00:41:34.810
I will open my heart to you.

00:41:36.140 --> 00:41:41.720
I always want to be able,

00:41:41.810 --> 00:41:45.880
To continue my search for you.
